Subject: Nurturing Pixie: do not refuse the creature because its bounce has no good target
Why: Before casting a creature the AI asks whether it would use each ETB trigger
  (AiController.checkETBEffects) and refuses the creature if not. ChangeZoneAi only likes
  bouncing opponents' permanents (or saving one of its own that is about to die), and Pixie can
  only return its controller's own, so the answer was almost always no (Azorius Momo, baseline:
  seen in 165 games, cast in 5). The BadETB escape does not apply to a TargetMin$ 0 trigger.
  OptionalDecider$ You makes the trigger optional, which plays out the same as "up to one
  target" choosing none: the AI now casts Pixie as a one-mana flier and still uses the bounce
  when it saves a threatened permanent. (A person playing it gets a yes/no prompt first.)
Measured: PENDING (filled in from the before/after gauntlets).

